/-- Filtered SU(7) weight-graph downward connectivity for one produced active
cell.

This is the next source-generation target in its decomposed representation
form.  It does not claim physical correctness of SU(7), and it does not assume
coverage/no-gap.  It records the exact checks that must hold before the
existing repair throat can fire:

* `completion_room`: endpoint room grows by a grammar-generated completion,
  not by replacing the active sector with an arbitrary broad box;
* `unit_quantization`: root/weight motion can be refined to a one-unit
  residual step, not merely a strict lower move of unknown size;
* `branching_filter_preserved`: after branching and filtering, the lower
  weight still lies in the generated no-prime sector;
* `root_move_strict_lower`: the weight/root move genuinely lowers the
  witness-local residual readout.

The dangerous mathematical point is the filtered connectedness field: Weyl or
root adjacency before filtering is not enough if the no-prime / endpoint /
code-bound filter cuts the path. -/
structure SU7FilteredWeightGraphDownwardConnectivity
    {K : Type*} [Field K] {σ : K} {hσ : σ ≠ 1}
    {n bound : ℕ}
    (A : SU7ProducedActiveCell σ hσ n bound) where
  completedBound : ℕ
  completion_room : bound ≤ completedBound
  unit_quantization :
    NoPrimeBranchingQuantizedUnitBridge
      (generatedNoPrimeBranchingCells n completedBound)
  lower : SU7NoPrimeBranchingSpectrumCell rawCodeTensorCoding n
  branching_filter_preserved :
    lower ∈ generatedNoPrimeBranchingCells n completedBound
  root_move_strict_lower :
    noPrimeBranchingEndpointResidualEnergy lower <
      noPrimeBranchingEndpointResidualEnergy
        (noPrimeBranchingCellOfBooleanAtomicRawCell A.sourceCell)

